{"variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/swiftpreprocessing\/hardwarerouterandmemory"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"topicSections":[{"title":"Memory & Routing APIs","identifiers":["doc:\/\/SwiftPreprocessing\/documentation\/SwiftPreprocessing\/HardwareRouter","doc:\/\/SwiftPreprocessing\/documentation\/SwiftPreprocessing\/WiredMemoryManager","doc:\/\/SwiftPreprocessing\/documentation\/SwiftPreprocessing\/WiredMemoryTicket"],"anchor":"Memory--Routing-APIs"}],"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"content","content":[{"text":"Overview","anchor":"Overview","level":2,"type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Apple Silicon features a "},{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Unified Memory Architecture (UMA)"}]},{"type":"text","text":" where the CPU, GPU, and Apple Neural Engine (ANE) share a single high-bandwidth memory pool. "},{"code":"SwiftPreprocessing","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" provides intelligent hardware routing and memory reservation primitives to prevent GPU saturation and avoid data copying."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"text":"1. The Hardware Router","anchor":"1-The-Hardware-Router","level":2,"type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The "},{"code":"HardwareRouter","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" assesses tensor dimensions and operation complexity to select the optimal computing engine:"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"syntax":"mermaid","code":["graph TD","    Op[Compute Operation] --> Router{HardwareRouter}","    Router -->|Small \/ Vector < 50k| CPU[Accelerate \/ AMX \/ NEON]","    Router -->|Large Matrix \/ Autodiff| GPU[MLX Metal GPU]","    Router -->|Static Inference| ANE[Core ML Engine]"],"type":"codeListing"},{"items":[{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Small Vectors ($N < 50{,}000$)"}]},{"type":"text","text":": Routed to CPU Accelerate (vDSP\/BLAS\/LAPACK) to eliminate GPU kernel dispatch latency."}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Large Tensors & Deep Learning"}]},{"type":"text","text":": Routed to MLX Metal GPU for massive parallel throughput."}],"type":"paragraph"}]}],"type":"unorderedList"},{"text":"2. WiredMemoryManager & Ticket System","anchor":"2-WiredMemoryManager--Ticket-System","level":2,"type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"To prevent out-of-memory (OOM) conditions during concurrent analytical workloads, "},{"code":"WiredMemoryManager","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" implements an asynchronous FIFO reservation system:"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"syntax":"swift","code":["import SwiftPreprocessing","","\/\/ Acquire a GPU execution slot","let ticket = try await WiredMemoryManager.shared.reserveMemory(estimatedBytes: 64 * 1024 * 1024)","","\/\/ Execute heavy MLX operations","\/\/ ...","","\/\/ Automatically flushes GPU caches upon completion","await ticket.release()"],"type":"codeListing"}]}],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Understand how SwiftSci automatically routes workloads between CPU (Accelerate\/AMX\/NEON) and Metal GPU (MLX) with strict concurrency safety."}],"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/SwiftPreprocessing\/documentation\/SwiftPreprocessing\/HardwareRouterAndMemory","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"sections":[],"schemaVersion":{"patch":0,"major":0,"minor":3},"metadata":{"title":"Hardware Routing & Unified Memory Governance","role":"collectionGroup","roleHeading":"API Collection","modules":[{"name":"SwiftPreprocessing"}]},"kind":"article","hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/SwiftPreprocessing\/documentation\/SwiftPreprocessing"]]},"references":{"doc://SwiftPreprocessing/documentation/SwiftPreprocessing":{"url":"\/documentation\/swiftpreprocessing","abstract":[{"text":"Feature Scaling, Categorical Encoders & Preprocessing Pipelines.","type":"text"}],"kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiftPreprocessing\/documentation\/SwiftPreprocessing","type":"topic","title":"Swi